  "name": "Real.rpow",
  "docstring": "The real power function `x ^ y`, defined as the real part of the complex power function.\nFor `x > 0`, it is equal to `exp (y log x)`. For `x = 0`, one sets `0 ^ 0=1` and `0 ^ y=0` for\n`y ≠ 0`. For `x < 0`, the definition is somewhat arbitrary as it depends on the choice of a complex\ndetermination of the logarithm. With our conventions, it is equal to `exp (y log x) cos (π y)`. "
}"}], "structured_content": {"result": {"id": 146059, "name": "Real.rpow", "docstring": "The real power function `x ^ y`, defined as the real part of the complex power function.
